  "title": "",
  "body": "  You are continually having troubles with the CRT screen of your computer and wonder if it is due to magnetic fields from the power lines running in your building. A blueprint of the building shows that the nearest power line is a thin wire that runs in a clockwise loop, wrapping around the outer perimeter of an arc-shaped hallway, as shown below.   replacement tag   replacement tag    Your CRT screen is located at point P. Calculate the magnetic field at P as a function of the current I and the distances a and b. Wire segments BC and AD are arcs of concentric circles. Wire segments AB and DC are straight-line segments.   "
